{"strongs": "H3801", "word": "כֻּתֹּ֫נֶת", "translit": "ke.to.net", "root": "כתנת", "morph": "H:N-F", "pos": "noun feminine", "gloss": "tunic", "definition": "כֻּתֹּ֫נֶת , כְּתֹ֫נֶת noun feminine tunic (Late Hebrew id. ; Aramaic כִּתּוּנָא . etc., etc.; Ethiopic tunic, linen ; compare also √ above); — absolute כֻּתֹּנֶת Gen 37:31 + 2 t.; כְּתֹנֶת Exod 28:39 construct כְּתֹנֶת Gen 37:3 + 9 t.; suffix כֻּתָּנְתּוֺ Gen 37:23 ; 2Sam 15:32 , כֻּתָּנְתֶּ֑ךָ Isa 22:21 , כֻּתָּנְתִּי Job 30:18 ; Song 5:3 plural absolute כֻּתֳּנֹת Exod 28:40 + 3 t., הַכָּתְנֹת Exod 39:27 construct כָּתְנוֺת Gen 3:21 + 2 t., כָּתְנֹת Ezra 2:69 suffix כֻּתֳּנֹתָם Lev 10:5 — tunic , principal ordinary garment (see Benz Archaeology 98 f. Now Archaeology i, 121, 193 ) of man and woman, worn next the person, כָּתְנֹת עוֺר Gen 3:21 tunics of skin ; of man 2Sam 15:32 ׳ פִּי כ Job 30:18 mouth of any tunic (i.e. its collar); פַּסִּים ׳ כ Gen 37:3 ; Gen 37:23 ; Gen 37:32 i.e. tunic with long skirts and sleeves (see פַּס ), compare v Gen 37:23 v Gen 37:31 v Gen 37:31 v Gen 37:32 v Gen 37:33 of woman Song 5:3 (put off at night); פַּסִּים ׳ כ 2Sam 13:18 ; 2Sam 13:19 (of king's daughter; rent, as sign of grief, compare also 2Sam 15:32 , and see קרע ). Specifically of priest's tunic Exod 28:4 ; Exod 28:39 (embroidered, see שׁבץ , תַּשְׁבֵּץ ), v Exod 28:40 ; Exod 29:5 ; Exod 29:8 ; Exod 39:27 (made of שֵׁשׁ , q. v.), Exod 40:14 ; Lev 8:7 ; Lev 8:13 ; Lev 10:5 בַּֿד קֹדֶשׁ ׳ כּ Lev 16:4 a holy linen tunic , of high priest; כֹּֿהֲנִים ׳ כ Ezra 2:69 ; Neh 7:69 ; Neh 7:71 ( van d. H. v Neh 7:70 v Neh 7:72 ); of Shebna's official tunic Isa 22:21 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4252')\">BDB4252</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3801')\">H3801</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4251')\">BDB4251</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4253')\">BDB4253</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>כֻּתֹּ֫נֶת</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>כְּתֹ֫נֶת</bdbheb> <b>noun feminine</b> <highl